# the outer keys (C3..E3, G#5..C6, past the FM-1's 27: app/smk37.c lsmk_outer) held with the keyboard's (ui.c
# outer_note): among the notes held, which Steps' head shows all of, low to high (a chord of six on poly: past the four a
# step takes, the sound's name gives way), what a step tapped takes, and step record's
wait 300
turn ALGO 2
wait 60
expect trk 3
outer 1 100
wait 40
expect held 1
expect rem1 49
outer 1 0
wait 40
expect held 0
expect rem1 49
# a chord of six: C#3 (outer), F3 A3 C4 E4 (keys), A#5 (outer)
outer 1 100
key 0 down
key 4 down
key 7 down
key 11 down
outer 7 100
wait 200
expect held 6
expect rem1 49
expect rem4 60
expect voices 6
shot outer_chord.png
outer 7 0
key 11 up
key 7 up
key 4 up
key 0 up
outer 1 0
wait 200
expect held 0
# a top key alone: B5
outer 8 100
wait 60
expect rem1 83
shot outer_top.png
outer 8 0
wait 60
# step record (REC tapped, stopped): an outer key writes the step, the cursor on
tap REC
wait 60
expect steprec 1
outer 8 100
wait 40
outer 8 0
wait 40
outer 1 100
wait 40
outer 1 0
wait 40
expect note 3 1 1 83
expect note 3 1 2 49
tap REC
wait 60
expect steprec 0
